 "result_text": "I made no changes. The issue is about a test assertion, and I'm not allowed to edit tests.\n\n`test_threshold` asserts `mod1 < mod2`, which is too strict. A larger `threshold` stops Louvain earlier, so it can only match or lower the modularity of the default run. For some graphs and seeds the two runs reach the same partition and the modularities are equal.\n\nI read `louvain_partitions` in `networkx/algorithms/community/louvain.py` and found no bug in it. It yields the current level's partition, then stops if the modularity gain is at or below `threshold`. I didn't run anything.\n\nThe fix the issue asks for is changing the assertion in `networkx/algorithms/community/tests/test_louvain.py` to `assert mod1 <= mod2`. Say if you want me to make that edit.",
